    "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Charleston SC",
    "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 27 at 2:23AM EDT until September 27 at 11:00AM EDT by NWS Charleston SC",
    "description": "* WHAT...Up to one half foot of inundation above ground level\nexpected along shorelines and tidal waterways (9.4 to 9.6 feet\nMean Lower Low Water at Fort Pulaski).\n\n* WHERE...Beaufort, Coastal Jasper, and coastal southeast\nGeorgia.\n\n* WHEN...From 7 AM to 11 AM EDT this morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Saltwater inundation will impact some roads.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...High tide will occur around 8:53 AM today\nat Fort Pulaski. Saltwater inundation will be possible 1 to 2\nhours before and after high tide.",
    "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.\n\nVisit water.weather.gov for additional water level and flood\nimpact information.",
    "response": "Monitor",
